.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM-ENCRYPT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm-encrypt \- encrypt a file or stdin with an encryption key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekm encrypt
.BR \-\-key\-id | \-k
.I KEY_ID
[\fB\-\-input\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-output\fR|\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Encrypts a file or, if
.B \-\-input
is omitted, standard input, with the given key and writes the
ciphertext to a file or, if
.B \-\-output
is omitted, standard output.
.PP
Unlike most
.B ekm
actions, the request and response bodies are raw bytes rather than
JSON: the plaintext travels as the request body and the ciphertext
comes back as the response body, both read and written in binary
mode. The key ID travels as a header instead of a JSON field.
.PP
Only a key whose status is
.B AVAILABLE
can be used to encrypt. A key that has been revoked (see
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-revoke-key (1))
or scheduled for deletion (see
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1))
still decrypts fine, but is rejected here with
.IR "HTTP 403" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key\-id " " \fIKEY_ID\fR
ID of the key to encrypt with, as returned by the
.B name
field of
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1).
Required.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIFILE\fR
Path of the file to encrypt. If omitted, the plaintext is read from
standard input.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to write the ciphertext to. If omitted, the ciphertext is
written to standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The data was encrypted; the ciphertext was written to the requested
destination.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the input or output file could not be
opened, the server could not be reached, or the server rejected the
request (e.g. unknown key ID).
.SH EXAMPLES
Encrypt a file to another file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm encrypt \e
    --key-id 3f1c2b7a-... --input plain.txt --output plain.enc
.fi
.RE
Encrypt stdin and write ciphertext to stdout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat plain.txt | euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 \e
    ekm encrypt --key-id 3f1c2b7a-... > plain.enc
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-revoke-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-decrypt (1)
